    <!-- 4. Groww Track -->
    <span class="verdict-pill pill-yellow">⚠️ Good for Groww users only</span>
    <h2>4. Groww Track</h2>
    <p>
      Groww Track lets you import external mutual fund holdings via CAS to see a consolidated mutual fund picture alongside your Groww investments. Convenient if you already invest through Groww.
    </p>
    <h3>Key strengths</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>Easy CAS-based import for external mutual funds</li>
      <li>XIRR and category allocation views</li>
      <li>Free with no subscription</li>
    </ul>
    <h3>Limitations</h3>
    <p>
      Stock tracking is limited to holdings purchased within Groww. If you use Zerodha, Angel One, or any other broker for stocks, those won't appear. No EPF, NPS, or FD support. See our full <a href="/arthavi-vs-groww">Arthavi vs. Groww comparison</a>.
    </p>
    <h3>Who should use it</h3>
    <p>Newer investors who invest primarily through Groww and want a basic consolidated MF view.</p>

    <!-- 5. MFCentral -->
    <span class="verdict-pill pill-green">✅ Best for authoritative MF data</span>
    <h2>5. MFCentral</h2>
    <p>
      MFCentral is a <strong>joint initiative by CAMS and KFintech</strong> — India's two dominant registrar and transfer agents for mutual funds. It gives you a regulated, authoritative view of all your mutual fund folios across every AMC.
    </p>
    <h3>Key strengths</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>Data comes directly from registrar records — highest possible MF data accuracy</li>
      <li>OTP + PAN verification only — no passwords required</li>
      <li>Submit service requests (nomination updates, contact changes) directly</li>
      <li>Completely free with no premium tier</li>
    </ul>
    <h3>Limitations</h3>
    <p>MFCentral covers <strong>mutual funds only</strong>. No stocks, FDs, NPS, or XIRR analytics. It's a viewing and servicing tool, not a full portfolio tracker.</p>
    <h3>Who should use it</h3>
    <p>Investors who want registrar-backed, authoritative mutual fund data and don't need broader tracking.</p>

    <!-- 6. Zerodha Console -->
    <span class="verdict-pill pill-yellow">⚠️ Zerodha users only</span>
    <h2>6. Zerodha Console</h2>
    <p>
      Zerodha Console is an excellent analytics platform — for your <strong>Zerodha holdings only</strong>. It provides detailed P&amp;L reports, XIRR, tax statements, and visualizations that are genuinely useful for active equity investors on the platform.
    </p>
    <h3>Limitations</h3>
    <p>
      No support for external broker holdings, CAS-based mutual fund imports, or any asset class outside Zerodha. See our <a href="/arthavi-vs-zerodha">Arthavi vs. Zerodha comparison</a> for a full breakdown.
    </p>
    <h3>Who should use it</h3>
    <p>Zerodha users who invest only on that platform and want deep analytics for their equity portfolio.</p>

    <!-- 7. Kuvera -->
    <span class="verdict-pill pill-green">✅ Good for MF + goals</span>
    <h2>7. Kuvera</h2>
    <p>
      Kuvera is a direct mutual fund investment platform with strong tracking and goal-based planning features. If you invest in mutual funds through Kuvera, the tracking experience is seamless.
    </p>
    <h3>Key strengths</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>Goal-based tracking and target allocation</li>
      <li>CAS import supported</li>
      <li>XIRR analytics and tax statements</li>
      <li>Free for direct fund investments</li>
    </ul>
    <h3>Limitations</h3>
    <p>Stock tracking is limited. Not suitable as an all-in-one net worth tracker with significant equity holdings outside the platform.</p>

    <!-- 8. ET Money -->
    <span class="verdict-pill pill-yellow">⚠️ Analytics locked behind paywall</span>
    <h2>8. ET Money (Genius)</h2>
    <p>
      ET Money started as a mutual fund investment and tracking app and has evolved into a broader financial platform. Its "Genius" tier unlocks AI-driven portfolio insights and recommendations.
    </p>
    <h3>Limitations</h3>
    <p>
      The best analytics — including portfolio health scores and XIRR breakdowns — require the paid Genius subscription. Stock tracking remains limited. Free tier functionality is comparable to most other free trackers.
    </p>
    <h3>Who should use it</h3>
    <p>Investors who want AI-driven MF insights and are willing to pay for the Genius tier.</p>

    <!-- 9. MProfit -->
    <span class="verdict-pill pill-blue">💼 Best for professionals / HNIs</span>
    <h2>9. MProfit</h2>
    <p>
      MProfit is a <strong>professional-grade portfolio management software</strong> used by IFAs, CA firms, and HNI investors. It covers the widest range of asset classes including stocks, mutual funds, PMS, AIF, real estate, and more.
    </p>
    <h3>Key strengths</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>Widest asset class coverage of any tracker on this list</li>
      <li>Professional tax reporting and capital gains statements</li>
      <li>Multi-client / multi-portfolio management</li>
      <li>No broker login required — import-based</li>
    </ul>
    <h3>Limitations</h3>
    <p>
      MProfit is <strong>not free</strong> — plans start at a few thousand rupees per year. The interface is feature-heavy and may feel complex for casual retail investors.
    </p>
    <h3>Who should use it</h3>
    <p>IFAs, CA firms, and HNI investors with complex multi-asset portfolios who need professional-grade reporting.</p>

    <!-- HOW TO CHOOSE -->
    <h2>How to Choose the Right Online Investment Tracker</h2>
    <p>Use this simple decision framework:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Want everything free + private + accurate XIRR?</strong> → <a href="https://app.arthavi.com/register">Arthavi</a></li>
      <li><strong>Want widest asset coverage (US stocks, EPF, credit cards)?</strong> → INDmoney (accept credential sharing)</li>
      <li><strong>Only mutual funds + deep research?</strong> → Value Research or Kuvera</li>
      <li><strong>Only Zerodha stocks?</strong> → Zerodha Console</li>
      <li><strong>Professional-grade multi-client reporting?</strong> → MProfit</li>
      <li><strong>Just want official MF data with zero setup?</strong> → MFCentral</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>Key features to demand from any online investment tracker</h3>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Accurate XIRR:</strong> Absolute returns lie. XIRR tells you the true annualised return factoring in every SIP date.</li>
      <li><strong>No credential sharing:</strong> Never give your broker password to a third-party app. Use <a href="/portfolio-tracker-without-broker-login">trackers that work without broker login</a>.</li>
      <li><strong>CAS-based import:</strong> The gold standard for mutual fund data accuracy in India.</li>
      <li><strong>Capital gains reporting:</strong> Especially important with LTCG on equity having a ₹1.25 lakh threshold.</li>
      <li><strong>Family portfolio support:</strong> Track multiple PANs if you manage family investments.</li>
    </ul>

