      <details class="faq-item" id="faq-xirr">
        <summary>What is XIRR and why does it matter for investment tracking?</summary>
        <div class="faq-body">
          XIRR (Extended Internal Rate of Return) is the true annualised return on your investment, calculated by accounting for the exact date and amount of every cash flow (SIP, lump sum, redemption). Absolute returns can be misleading for SIP investors — XIRR is the only metric that tells you what your money actually earned per year. Use Arthavi's <a href="/xirr-calculator-mutual-funds">XIRR calculator</a> to check any investment.
        </div>
